  "id": "COMPOUND:223 - PROTEIN:685",
  "verbalization": "Aminosalicylic acid appears to interact with Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Aminosalicylic acid acts as a target of Quinaldic Acid and Diacylglycerol kinase gamma, which in turn targets the phosphatase subunit. This implies a potential pathway where Aminosalicylic acid may influence the activity of Diacylglycerol kinase gamma, which then affects the phosphatase subunit. The shared involvement of the phosphatase subunit in multiple pathways indicates a possible functional link, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where Aminosalicylic acid indirectly influences the phosphatase subunit through its targets, but the precise nature of this interaction requires further investigation.",
